--TEST--
inside a string literal at a `Core` member's path parameter the list is what the directory its text reaches holds, resolved against the document's own directory as the compiler resolves the literal: each directory with a `/` after it and every file, whatever its extension, and no name that starts with a `.` — `rule:programs/path-literals-resolve-from-their-file`
--FILE--
<?nvs
echo Core\IO::read('data/<|>');
--FILE data/config.json--
{}
--FILE data/notes.txt--
notes
--FILE data/archive/old.txt--
old
--FILE data/.hidden--
hidden
--REQUEST--
completion
--EXPECT--
archive/ folder
config.json file
notes.txt file
